    "Notebook" -> "974e939a-7268-4f58-b7f9-95898cc3d9dd"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> ".md\nHere we convert from Cartesian coordinates to spherical \
(more precisely, geodetic) coordinates\n\n$$\n\\\\begin{matrix}\n\nlat =& \
90^\\\\circ - arccos(z/r) \\\\\\\\\nlon =& \
arctan(x/y)\n\\\\end{matrix}\n$$\n\nwe retrieve the elevations and normalize \
them.  \n\nThe final step is to link them back to the original points on the \
sphere, using the normalized elevation as the distance along the normal.  ", 
    "Display" -> "codemirror", "Hash" -> 
     "072a5ecc-7693-4415-9329-0d2809206fea", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <|"Hidden" -> True|>, 
    "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Input", 
    "UID" -> Null, "Notebook" -> "974e939a-7268-4f58-b7f9-95898cc3d9dd"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> "Here we convert from Cartesian coordinates to spherical (more \
precisely, geodetic) coordinates\n\n$$\n\\\\begin{matrix}\n\nlat =& \
90^\\\\circ - arccos(z/r) \\\\\\\\\nlon =& \
arctan(x/y)\n\\\\end{matrix}\n$$\n\nwe retrieve the elevations and normalize \
them.  \n\nThe final step is to link them back to the original points on the \
sphere, using the normalized elevation as the distance along the normal.  ", 
    "Display" -> "markdown", "Hash" -> 
     "165620b1-1590-4808-865c-9a5a184c1e72", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <||>, "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, 
