   <|"Data" -> ".md\n## Generating clouds\nWhat\[CloseCurlyQuote]s Earth \
without clouds? And what are clouds without Perlin noise?  \n\nThe next piece \
I honestly stole from one of the forums (no GPT for you!)", 
    "Display" -> "codemirror", "Hash" -> 
     "3cdb4cba-bcb4-4b7a-9918-55fdc0a79f4e", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <|"Hidden" -> True|>, 
    "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Input", 
    "UID" -> Null, "Notebook" -> "974e939a-7268-4f58-b7f9-95898cc3d9dd"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> "## Generating clouds\nWhat\[CloseCurlyQuote]s Earth without \
clouds? And what are clouds without Perlin noise?  \n\nThe next piece I \
honestly stole from one of the forums (no GPT for you!)", 
    "Display" -> "markdown", "Hash" -> 
     "03163bce-7ae4-453c-b8b9-4a6581cb598a", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <||>, "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, 
    "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Output", "UID" -> Null, 
    "Notebook" -> "974e939a-7268-4f58-b7f9-95898cc3d9dd"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> "n = 256;\nratio = 1/2;\n\nk2 = Outer[Plus, #, #] \
&[RotateRight[N@Range[-n, n - 1, 2]/n, n/2]^2];\n\nk2 = k2[[;; ;; 1/ratio, \
All]];\n\nspectrum = With[{d := RandomReal[NormalDistribution[], {n ratio, \
n}]},\n   (1/n) (d)/(0.001 + k2)]; \nspectrum[[1, 1]] *= 0;\n\nim[p_] := \
Clip[Re[InverseFourier[spectrum Exp[I p]]], {0, \[Infinity]}]^0.5\n\np0 = p = \
Sqrt[k2];\ncloudTexture = Image[im[p0 += p], Magnification->2]", 
    "Display" -> "codemirror", "Hash" -> 
     "aa63a940-6ba0-493a-827b-53737ca1f7e6", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <||>, "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, 
    "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Input", "UID" -> Null, 
    "Notebook" -> "974e939a-7268-4f58-b7f9-95898cc3d9dd"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> "(*VB[*)(FrontEndRef[\"458950d1-e7da-4def-ab37-b7e33e1e1360\"]\
)(*,*)(*\"1:eJxTTMoPSmNkYGAoZgESHvk5KRCeEJBwK8rPK3HNS3GtSE0uLUlMykkNVgEKm5haW\
JoapBjqppqnJOqapKSm6SYmGZvrJpmnGhunGqYaGpsZAACHqRXR\"*)(*]VB*)", 
    "Display" -> "codemirror", "Hash" -> 
     "5250bf87-84b8-406f-9e29-9658fe9b7d2e", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <||>, "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, 
    "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Output", "UID" -> Null, 
    "Notebook" -> "974e939a-7268-4f58-b7f9-95898cc3d9dd"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> ".md\nHere animated version", "Display" -> "codemirror", 
    "Hash" -> "99c60add-6d2f-4edf-9209-dfcc0bee51e0", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <|"Hidden" -> True|>, 
    "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Input", 
    "UID" -> Null, "Notebook" -> "974e939a-7268-4f58-b7f9-95898cc3d9dd"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> "Here animated version", "Display" -> "markdown", 
    "Hash" -> "515ab05f-e0d5-4361-a5e6-c40581a03397", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <||>, "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, 
    "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Output", "UID" -> Null, 
    "Notebook" -> "974e939a-7268-4f58-b7f9-95898cc3d9dd"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> "Refresh[Image[im[p0 += p]], 0.1]", "Display" -> "codemirror", 
    "Hash" -> "8ff504fe-0e16-49f7-ad37-440920bdb2db", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <||>, "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, 
    "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Input", "UID" -> Null, 
    "Notebook" -> "974e939a-7268-4f58-b7f9-95898cc3d9dd"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> ".md\nHow do we make them three-dimensional? I \
couldn\[CloseCurlyQuote]t think of anything better than using the Marching \
Cubes technique to generate low-poly clouds.  \n\nHowever, to start, \
we\[CloseCurlyQuote]ll \"stretch\" the 2D image into 3D with fading at the \
edges.  ", "Display" -> "codemirror", 
    "Hash" -> "f6c2d6f3-a4ab-477a-a747-257a93a1796b", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <|"Hidden" -> True|>, 
    "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Input", 
    "UID" -> Null, "Notebook" -> "974e939a-7268-4f58-b7f9-95898cc3d9dd"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> "How do we make them three-dimensional? I \
couldn\[CloseCurlyQuote]t think of anything better than using the Marching \
Cubes technique to generate low-poly clouds.  \n\nHowever, to start, \
we\[CloseCurlyQuote]ll \"stretch\" the 2D image into 3D with fading at the \
edges.  ", "Display" -> "markdown", 
    "Hash" -> "94173d40-832f-43d8-98b7-b21f8ff69141", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <||>, "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, 
    "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Output", "UID" -> Null, 
    "Notebook" -> "974e939a-7268-4f58-b7f9-95898cc3d9dd"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> "With[{plain = im[p0+=p]}, Table[plain Exp[-( i)^2/200.], {i, \
-20,20}]][[;;;;8, ;;;;4, ;;;;4]] // Image3D ", "Display" -> "codemirror", 
    "Hash" -> "929e3aa8-eae7-4113-b0e6-2920a560f1cc", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <||>, "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, 
    "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Input", "UID" -> Null, 
    "Notebook" -> "974e939a-7268-4f58-b7f9-95898cc3d9dd"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> ".md\n*this is not an image, try to drag*\n\nTo turn this \
scalar field into polygons, we can use the `ImageMesh` function. However, \
it's quite challenging to work with when nonlinear transformations need to be \
applied to the mesh. And we will need to do these transformations, otherwise, \
how will we map this square onto the sphere?\n\nLet\[CloseCurlyQuote]s use an \
external library, `wl-marchingcubes`.  ", "Display" -> "codemirror", 
    "Hash" -> "ba82516e-c7f2-4fde-a254-4e09e6d4d27b", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <|"Hidden" -> True|>, 
    "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Input", 
    "UID" -> Null, "Notebook" -> "974e939a-7268-4f58-b7f9-95898cc3d9dd"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> "*this is not an image, try to drag*\n\nTo turn this scalar \
field into polygons, we can use the `ImageMesh` function. However, it's quite \
challenging to work with when nonlinear transformations need to be applied to \
the mesh. And we will need to do these transformations, otherwise, how will \
we map this square onto the sphere?\n\nLet\[CloseCurlyQuote]s use an external \
library, `wl-marchingcubes`.  ", "Display" -> "markdown", 
    "Hash" -> "1bfb35a5-213c-4662-abaf-938961ec7b81", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <||>, "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, 
    "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Output", "UID" -> Null, 
    "Notebook" -> "974e939a-7268-4f58-b7f9-95898cc3d9dd"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> "LPMRepositories[{\n    \"Github\" -> \
\"https://github.com/JerryI/wl-marching-cubes\" -> \
\"master\"\n}]\n\n<<JerryI`MarchingCubes`", "Display" -> "codemirror", 
    "Hash" -> "35655e4a-f101-44d6-9820-784725fea0e4", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <||>, "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, 
    "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Input", "UID" -> Null, 
    "Notebook" -> "974e939a-7268-4f58-b7f9-95898cc3d9dd"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> "With[{plain = im[p0]}, Table[plain Exp[-( i)^2/200.], {i, \
-20,20}]];\n\n{vertices, normals} = CMarchingCubes[%, 0.2];", 
    "Display" -> "codemirror", "Hash" -> 
     "58821942-b6e9-43ff-b029-d576385f8daa", "Invisible" -> False, 
