   <|"Data" -> "GraphicsComplex[vertices, Polygon[1, Length[vertices]]] // \
Graphics3D // Rasterize", "Display" -> "codemirror", 
    "Hash" -> "f98dba99-1ad9-486f-9925-639eb98acd5a", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <||>, "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, 
    "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Input", "UID" -> Null, 
    "Notebook" -> "974e939a-7268-4f58-b7f9-95898cc3d9dd"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> "(*VB[*)(FrontEndRef[\"cfb9bd1c-2faf-4461-bd21-dc626c96fda0\"]\
)(*,*)(*\"1:eJxTTMoPSmNkYGAoZgESHvk5KRCeEJBwK8rPK3HNS3GtSE0uLUlMykkNVgEKJ6clW\
SalGCbrGqUlpumamJgZ6ialGBnqpiSbGZklW5qlpSQaAACbJhaK\"*)(*]VB*)", 
    "Display" -> "codemirror", "Hash" -> 
     "20882df2-af6a-44be-a46f-0eb7a0073f4a", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <||>, "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, 
    "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Output", "UID" -> Null, 
    "Notebook" -> "974e939a-7268-4f58-b7f9-95898cc3d9dd"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> ".md\n\n### Mapping things to a sphere\n\nI'll mention right \
away that I\[CloseCurlyQuote]m not an expert in geodesy (@JerryI), but \
I\[CloseCurlyQuote]ve \"heard\" about some concepts from computational \
geometry and 3D graphics.\n\nIn any case, we\[CloseCurlyQuote]ll be \
\"mapping\" this texture onto the sphere in one form or another (as \
polygons). This means we\[CloseCurlyQuote]ll transform all its points \
following one of the cartographic projections. \n\nLooking at textures from \
games, we can notice a \
pattern\n\n![](/attachments/image-372.png)\n\n*https://richardrosenman.com/sh\
op/spherical-mapping-corrector/*\n\n<br/>\n\nAt the edges of the texture \
projected from the sphere, the details stretch towards the top and bottom \
edges of the rectangle. This is exactly the case when $ \\theta \
\\\\rightarrow 0, \\\\pi $ or $ v \\\\rightarrow 0, 1 $ \[LongDash] our \
poles.\n\nThus, if we artificially distort the original texture in the same \
way, we should eliminate the artifacts at the poles. Do you know what this \
transformation resembles?\n\nIt\[CloseCurlyQuote]s akin to transforming [the \
Mollweide projection into an equal-area cartographic \
projection](https://mathematica.stackexchange.com/a/79868/53728)", 
    "Display" -> "codemirror", "Hash" -> 
     "4a371559-0979-4516-b71d-3435ad181daa", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <|"Hidden" -> True|>, 
    "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Input", 
    "UID" -> Null, "Notebook" -> "974e939a-7268-4f58-b7f9-95898cc3d9dd"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> "\n### Mapping things to a sphere\n\nI'll mention right away \
that I\[CloseCurlyQuote]m not an expert in geodesy (@JerryI), but \
I\[CloseCurlyQuote]ve \"heard\" about some concepts from computational \
geometry and 3D graphics.\n\nIn any case, we\[CloseCurlyQuote]ll be \
\"mapping\" this texture onto the sphere in one form or another (as \
polygons). This means we\[CloseCurlyQuote]ll transform all its points \
following one of the cartographic projections. \n\nLooking at textures from \
games, we can notice a \
pattern\n\n![](/attachments/image-372.png)\n\n*https://richardrosenman.com/sh\
op/spherical-mapping-corrector/*\n\n<br />\n\nAt the edges of the texture \
projected from the sphere, the details stretch towards the top and bottom \
edges of the rectangle. This is exactly the case when $ \\theta \
\\\\rightarrow 0, \\\\pi $ or $ v \\\\rightarrow 0, 1 $ \[LongDash] our \
poles.\n\nThus, if we artificially distort the original texture in the same \
way, we should eliminate the artifacts at the poles. Do you know what this \
transformation resembles?\n\nIt\[CloseCurlyQuote]s akin to transforming [the \
Mollweide projection into an equal-area cartographic \
projection](https://mathematica.stackexchange.com/a/79868/53728)", 
    "Display" -> "markdown", "Hash" -> 
     "2b7eade7-f97c-44d9-9e37-bc0ed6ecc077", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <||>, "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, 
    "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Output", "UID" -> Null, 
    "Notebook" -> "974e939a-7268-4f58-b7f9-95898cc3d9dd"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> "lat[y_, rad_:1] := ArcSin[(2 theta[y, rad] + Sin[2 theta[y, \
rad]])/Pi];\nlon[x_, y_, rad_:1, lonzero_: 0] := lonzero + Pi x/(2 rad \
Sqrt[2] Cos[theta[y, rad]]);\ntheta[y_, rad_:1] := ArcSin[y/(rad \
Sqrt[2])];\nmollweidetoequirect[{x_, y_}] := {lon[x, y, 1], \
lat[y]};\n\nnewCloudTexture = ImageForwardTransformation[\n  cloudTexture,\n  \
mollweidetoequirect,\n  DataRange -> {{-2 Sqrt[2], 2 Sqrt[2]}, {-Sqrt[2], \
Sqrt[2]}},\n  PlotRange -> All\n];\n\nImage[%, Magnification->2]", 
    "Display" -> "codemirror", "Hash" -> 
     "2f0134e0-d716-472a-9b8e-b6cc6eaa0d7a", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <||>, "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, 
    "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Input", "UID" -> Null, 
    "Notebook" -> "974e939a-7268-4f58-b7f9-95898cc3d9dd"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> "(*VB[*)(FrontEndRef[\"0b3b02ec-63c8-4c7b-ab43-74a8dcfff90a\"]\
)(*,*)(*\"1:eJxTTMoPSmNkYGAoZgESHvk5KRCeEJBwK8rPK3HNS3GtSE0uLUlMykkNVgEKGyQZJ\
xkYpSbrmhknW+iaJJsn6SYmmRjrmpskWqQkp6WlWRokAgCLfRZZ\"*)(*]VB*)", 
    "Display" -> "codemirror", "Hash" -> 
     "a502a828-0366-47b6-b304-a4ed67e3b14a", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <||>, "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, 
    "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Output", "UID" -> Null, 
    "Notebook" -> "974e939a-7268-4f58-b7f9-95898cc3d9dd"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> ".md\nNext, we simply need to repeat Marching Cubes on it and \
transform all the vertices using the equation above. As a bonus, let's \
transform `normals` as well!", "Display" -> "codemirror", 
    "Hash" -> "2da4ab90-cba2-4371-a6c8-390115674cb2", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <|"Hidden" -> True|>, 
    "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Input", 
    "UID" -> Null, "Notebook" -> "974e939a-7268-4f58-b7f9-95898cc3d9dd"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> "Next, we simply need to repeat Marching Cubes on it and \
transform all the vertices using the equation above. As a bonus, let's \
transform `normals` as well!", "Display" -> "markdown", 
    "Hash" -> "b88eaad4-3cac-4a88-91b6-cca22896a480", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <||>, "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, 
    "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Output", "UID" -> Null, 
    "Notebook" -> "974e939a-7268-4f58-b7f9-95898cc3d9dd"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> "With[{plain = ImageData[ImageResize[newCloudTexture, \
Scaled[1/2]]]}, Table[plain Exp[-( i)^2/200.], {i, -20,20,2}]];\n\n{vertices, \
normals} = CMarchingCubes[%, 0.2];\n\nvertices = With[{\n  offset = \
{Min[vertices[[All,1]]], Min[vertices[[All,2]]], 0},\n  maxX = \
Max[vertices[[All,1]]] - Min[vertices[[All,1]]],\n  maxY = \
Max[vertices[[All,2]]] - Min[vertices[[All,2]]]\n}, Map[Function[v, With[{p = \
v - offset}, {p[[1]]/maxX, p[[2]]/maxY, p[[3]]}]], vertices]];\n\n{pvertices, \
pnormals} = MapThread[Function[{v,n},\n    With[{\\[Rho] = 50.0 + 0.25 \
(v[[3]] - 10), \\[Phi] =  2 Pi Clip[v[[1]], {0,1}], \\[Theta] =  Pi \
Clip[v[[2]], {0,1}]},\n      {\n        {\\[Rho] Cos[\\[Phi]] Sin[\\[Theta]], \
\\[Rho] Sin[\\[Phi]] Sin[\\[Theta]], \\[Rho] Cos[\\[Theta]]},\n\n        \
n[[3]] {Cos[\\[Phi]] Sin[\\[Theta]], Sin[\\[Phi]] Sin[\\[Theta]], \
Cos[\\[Theta]]} + \n        n[[2]] {Cos[\\[Theta]] \
Cos[\\[Phi]],Cos[\\[Theta]] Sin[\\[Phi]],-Sin[\\[Theta]]} + \n        n[[1]] \
{-Sin[\\[Theta]] Sin[\\[Phi]],Cos[\\[Phi]] Sin[\\[Theta]],0}\n      }\n    \
]\n  ]\n, {vertices, -normals}] // Transpose;\n\n{\n  clouds = \
GraphicsComplex[0.017 pvertices, Polygon[1, Length[vertices]], \
VertexNormals->pnormals]\n} // Graphics3D // Rasterize ", 
    "Display" -> "codemirror", "Hash" -> 
     "90a3b4d9-4369-4046-ac32-08cf1b519065", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <||>, "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, 
    "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Input", "UID" -> Null, 
    "Notebook" -> "974e939a-7268-4f58-b7f9-95898cc3d9dd"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> "(*VB[*)(FrontEndRef[\"ce398396-cbb9-4bac-b178-ed6a91941a07\"]\
)(*,*)(*\"1:eJxTTMoPSmNkYGAoZgESHvk5KRCeEJBwK8rPK3HNS3GtSE0uLUlMykkNVgEKJ6caW\
1oYW5rpJiclWeqaJCUm6yYZmlvopqaYJVoaWpoYJhqYAwCNnBXd\"*)(*]VB*)", 
    "Display" -> "codemirror", "Hash" -> 
     "a4d8cb2c-e174-47d4-acba-832c9210e244", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <||>, "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, 
    "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Output", "UID" -> Null, 
    "Notebook" -> "974e939a-7268-4f58-b7f9-95898cc3d9dd"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> ".md\nIf `VertexNormals` is explicitly set in \
`GraphicsComplex`, then when shading, the surface will be interpolated across \
all three normals of the triangle, instead of just one (which is \
automatically calculated by the graphics library if no other data is \
provided, in which case the polygon looks like a flat plane \[LongDash] \
a.k.a. the effect seen in 80s demos).  ", "Display" -> "codemirror", 
    "Hash" -> "c7cfda0b-7cae-49f0-a36c-3308820aa4f9", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <|"Hidden" -> True|>, 
    "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Input", 
    "UID" -> Null, "Notebook" -> "974e939a-7268-4f58-b7f9-95898cc3d9dd"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> "If `VertexNormals` is explicitly set in `GraphicsComplex`, \
then when shading, the surface will be interpolated across all three normals \
of the triangle, instead of just one (which is automatically calculated by \
the graphics library if no other data is provided, in which case the polygon \
looks like a flat plane \[LongDash] a.k.a. the effect seen in 80s demos).  ", 
    "Display" -> "markdown", "Hash" -> 
     "7cf6d57e-84f9-48ca-b5fe-8b809a25b789", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <||>, "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, 
    "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Output", "UID" -> Null, 
    "Notebook" -> "974e939a-7268-4f58-b7f9-95898cc3d9dd"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> ".md\n## Putting it all together\nWe can extend the original \
`SurfacePlot` with options and add additional graphic primitives through \
them. Oh, and don\[CloseCurlyQuote]t forget to turn off the default lighting. \
After all, we\[CloseCurlyQuote]re in space!  ", "Display" -> "codemirror", 
    "Hash" -> "82658e8a-2131-4a65-8e5d-b1be51590de3", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <|"Hidden" -> True|>, 
    "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Input", 
    "UID" -> Null, "Notebook" -> "974e939a-7268-4f58-b7f9-95898cc3d9dd"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> "## Putting it all together\nWe can extend the original \
`SurfacePlot` with options and add additional graphic primitives through \
them. Oh, and don\[CloseCurlyQuote]t forget to turn off the default lighting. \
After all, we\[CloseCurlyQuote]re in space!  ", "Display" -> "markdown", 
    "Hash" -> "c1d997ae-aa62-429f-9eda-007efc15feb1", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <||>, "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, 
    "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Output", "UID" -> Null, 
    "Notebook" -> "974e939a-7268-4f58-b7f9-95898cc3d9dd"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> "rainbow = ColorData[\"DarkRainbow\"];\n\nListSurfacePlot3D[\n \
 MapThread[(#1 (0.8 + 0.1 #2))&, {points, elevation}], \n  Mesh->None, \
MaxPlotPoints->50, \n  ColorFunction -> Function[{x,y,z}, rainbow[1.5(2 \
Norm[{x,y,z}]-1)]], \n  ColorFunctionScaling -> False, \n  Lighting->None,\n  \
PlotStyle->Directive[\"Shadows\"->True, \"CastShadow\"->True],\n\n  Prolog -> \
{\n    Directive[\"Shadows\"->True, \"CastShadow\"->True],\n    clouds,\n    \
HemisphereLight[LightBlue, Orange // Darker // Darker],\n    \
SpotLight[Orange, {-2.4909, 4.069, 3.024}]\n  },\n  \n  Background->Black,\n  \
Axes->False\n, ImageSize->600]\n", "Display" -> "codemirror", 
    "Hash" -> "480cbf29-47f6-44b6-b36b-80e77a2a3267", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <||>, "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, 
    "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Input", "UID" -> Null, 
    "Notebook" -> "974e939a-7268-4f58-b7f9-95898cc3d9dd"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> "(*VB[*)(FrontEndRef[\"6927cbfd-deef-4b74-80d6-7a9e3fbca385\"]\
)(*,*)(*\"1:eJxTTMoPSmNkYGAoZgESHvk5KRCeEJBwK8rPK3HNS3GtSE0uLUlMykkNVgEKm1kam\
ScnpaXopqSmpumaJJmb6FoYpJjpmidaphqnJSUnGluYAgCVohZ2\"*)(*]VB*)", 
    "Display" -> "codemirror", "Hash" -> 
     "83972306-08f1-4537-b7b4-aa60b929d4fb", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <||>, "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, 
    "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Output", "UID" -> Null, 
    "Notebook" -> "974e939a-7268-4f58-b7f9-95898cc3d9dd"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> ".md\n\n## Animation  \nLet\[CloseCurlyQuote]s add a simple \
animation for the movement of the light source, as well as the rotation of \
the cloud sphere to spice up the scene", "Display" -> "codemirror", 
    "Hash" -> "efbf7793-68e4-4355-ad0f-efb66fc7b4b7", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <|"Hidden" -> True|>, 
    "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Input", 
    "UID" -> Null, "Notebook" -> "974e939a-7268-4f58-b7f9-95898cc3d9dd"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> "\n## Animation  \nLet\[CloseCurlyQuote]s add a simple \
animation for the movement of the light source, as well as the rotation of \
the cloud sphere to spice up the scene", "Display" -> "markdown", 
    "Hash" -> "5f1a3fb7-a850-4195-aa96-744e6eee9616", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <||>, "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, 
    "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Output", "UID" -> Null, 
    "Notebook" -> "974e939a-7268-4f58-b7f9-95898cc3d9dd"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> "rainbow = ColorData[\"DarkRainbow\"];\nlightPos = {-2.4909, \
4.069, 3.024};\n\nrotationMatrix = RotationMatrix[0., {0,0,1}];\nangle = \
0.;\n\n\nListSurfacePlot3D[\n  MapThread[(#1 (0.8 + 0.1 #2))&, {points, \
elevation}], \n  Mesh->None, MaxPlotPoints->100, \n  ColorFunction -> \
Function[{x,y,z}, rainbow[1.5(2 Norm[{x,y,z}]-1)]], \n  ColorFunctionScaling \
-> False, \n  Lighting->\"Default\",\n  \
PlotStyle->Directive[\"Shadows\"->True, \"CastShadow\"->True],\n\n  Prolog -> \
{\n    Directive[\"Shadows\"->True, \"CastShadow\"->True],\n    \
GeometricTransformation[clouds, rotationMatrix // Offload],\n    \
HemisphereLight[LightBlue, Orange // Darker // Darker],\n    \
SpotLight[Orange, lightPos // Offload]\n  },\n\n  Epilog -> \
EventHandler[AnimationFrameListener[lightPos // Offload], Function[Null,\n    \
lightPos = RotationMatrix[1 Degree, {1,1,1}].lightPos;\n    rotationMatrix = \
RotationMatrix[angle, {0,0,1}];\n    angle += 0.5 Degree;    \n  ]],\n  \
Background->Black,\n  ImageSize->600\n]", "Display" -> "codemirror", 
    "Hash" -> "42a7a5e1-0a75-4bc3-b08f-6a4deeee26b2", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <||>, "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, 
    "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Input", "UID" -> Null, 
    "Notebook" -> "974e939a-7268-4f58-b7f9-95898cc3d9dd"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> ".md\nTo start animation", "Display" -> "codemirror", 
    "Hash" -> "41546b8d-0154-4e35-9f86-cc15763a9a7a", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <|"Hidden" -> True|>, 
    "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Input", 
